# Atlas core constraints

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), [architecture ownership](../../docs/how-we-build/architecture-ownership.md), and resolve [atlas.config.json](../../atlas.config.json) via `@atlas/project` before architectural changes. Inspect the closest example page (`apps/web/src/app/examples/`) or reference feature (`apps/web/src/features/reference/`) before writing code.

- **Ownership** — Product code stays in `apps/web`. Reference code lives in `features/reference/`, `components/reference/`, and `/examples`. Reusable visual primitives go in `@atlas/ui`. Do not promote code to shared packages speculatively.
- **API** — Use `@/lib/api` / `@/lib/api/contracts` and React Query hooks in feature modules. No raw `fetch()` in pages, components, features, or providers.
- **Config** — Use `useConfig()` or `getServerConfig()` from `@/config`. No direct `process.env` or `@/env` in application code.
- **States** — Every data-driven UI handles loading, empty, error, and success. Use `SkeletonList`, `EmptyState`, `ErrorFallback` from `@atlas/ui`.
- **Forms** — Use `useZodForm`, `FormField`, and `applyServerFieldErrors` from `@atlas/ui`.
- **Quality** — Preserve accessibility (semantic HTML, labels, keyboard, focus-visible) and responsive layout. No unnecessary dependencies or unrelated refactors.
- **Done means verified** — Run relevant checks before completion: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, and `pnpm build` when appropriate.
